{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'id: MONDO:10602' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo\"","aggregated_output":"[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060200\nname: primary hyperthyroidism\ndef: \"A form of hyperthyroidism caused by overproduction of thyroid hormones (T3 and T4) due to pathology within the thyroid gland itself. Primary hyperthyroidism is characterized by low TSH levels and elevated T3/T4 levels.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:30725738]\nxref: MEDGEN:811409 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C3714618 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:811409\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0004425 {source=\"PMID:30725738\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! hyperthyroidism\nintersection_of: MONDO:0004425 ! hyperthyroidism\nintersection_of: disease_has_basis_in_dysfunction_of UBERON:0002046 ! thyroid gland\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9759\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060201\nname: secondary hyperthyroidism\ndef: \"A form of hyperthyroidism caused by overproduction of thyroid hormones (T3 and T4) due to pathology outside of the thyroid gland, namely in the hypothalamus or pituitary gland. Secondary hyperthyroidism is characterized by elevated TSH levels and elevated T3/T4 levels.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:30725738]\nxref: MEDGEN:923144 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C1095928 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:923144\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0004425 {source=\"PMID:30725738\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! hyperthyroidism\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9759\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060202\nname: toxic thyroid adenoma\ndef: \"A condition in which a single benign adenoma on the thyroid gland  autonomously secretes excessive thyroid hormone, leading to primary hyperthyroidism.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:30725738]\nsubset: inferred_rare\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"toxic adenoma\" EXACT [PMID:30725738]\nxref: MEDGEN:549890 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0302840 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:549890\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005032 {source=\"PMID:32965923\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! follicular thyroid adenoma\nis_a: MONDO:1060200 {source=\"PMID:30725738\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! primary hyperthyroidism\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9759\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060203\nname: hypothalamic hyperthyroidism\ndef: \"A form of secondary hyperthyroidism caused by pathology in the hypothalamus leading to excessive stimulation of the pituitary gland and subsequent overproduction of TSH, resulting in elevated thyroid hormone levels.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:30725738]\nis_a: MONDO:1060201 {source=\"PMID:30725738\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! secondary hyperthyroidism\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9759\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060204\nname: menstrual disorder\ndef: \"A disorder of the female reproductive system characterized by abnormalities in the menstrual cycle, including disturbances in timing, flow, or associated pain.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:29489290, PMID:32809669]\nis_a: MONDO:0002263 {source=\"PMID:29489290\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! female reproductive system disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060205\nname: dysmenorrhea\ndef: \"A menstrual disorder characterized by pain during the menstrual cycle.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/dysmenorrhea-painful-periods, PMID:32809669]\nxref: MEDGEN:4429 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0013390 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:4429\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1060204 {source=\"PMID:32809669\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! menstrual disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060206\nname: primary dysmenorrhea\ndef: \"A form of dysmenorrhea characterized by recurrent menstrual pain without any identifiable underlying pelvic pathology, representing a diagnosis of exclusion. Symptoms typically emerge within two years of menarche.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:32809669]\nxref: MEDGEN:508446 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0149875 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:508446\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1060205 {source=\"PMID:32809669\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! dysmenorrhea\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060207\nname: secondary dysmenorrhea\ndef: \"A form of dysmenorrhea associated with suspected or clinically identifiable pelvic pathology, such as endometriosis, uterine fibroids, or adenomyosis.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:32809669]\nxref: MEDGEN:534931 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0232944 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MEDGEN:534931\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1060205 {source=\"PMID:32809669\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! dysmenorrhea\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060208\nname: primary amenorrhea\ndef: \"A form of amenorrhea defined by the absence of menstruation by the age of 15 years, or by 3 years after the onset of breast development (thelarche).\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:29489290]\nxref: MEDGEN:115918 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0232939 {source=\"MEDGEN:115918\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0001836 {source=\"PMID:29489290\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! amenorrhea\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060209\nname: secondary amenorrhea\ndef: \"A form of amenorrhea characterized by the absence of menses for 3 or more months in a woman with previously regular menstrual cycles, or 6 or more months in any woman who has had at least one previous spontaneous menstruation.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:29489290]\nxref: MEDGEN:115919 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0232940 {source=\"MEDGEN:115919\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0001836 {source=\"PMID:29489290\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! amenorrhea\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060210\nname: functional hypothalamic amenorrhea\ndef: \"A form of secondary amenorrhea caused by suppression of the hypothalamic-pituitary-ovarian axis without identifiable organic pathology, typically associated with energy deficiency, excessive exercise, psychological stress, or low body weight.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:29489290]\nis_a: MONDO:1060209 {source=\"PMID:29489290\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! secondary amenorrhea\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060211\nname: NR5A1-related sex development disorder\ndef: \"A reproductive system disorder caused by a variation in the NR5A1 gene, and characterized by varying phenotypes, including partial or complete gonadal dysgenesis, ambiguous genitalia, and spermatogenic failure in the male, and premature ovarian failure and ovarian dysgenesis in the female.\" [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/, PMID:28033660, PMID:31513305]\ncomment: 46XY individuals can present with azoospermia, hypospadias, micropenis, cryptorchidism, ambiguous or female-appearing genitalia, partial or complete gonadal dysgenesis, Sertoli dysfunction, and progressive testicular failure. Leydig function is often partially preserved, and infertility is common. 46XX individuals can present with primary ovarian insufficiency/ premature ovarian failure, ovarian dysgenesis, and subfertility. Rarely, testicular or ovotesticular disorder of sex development may occur. Individuals typically have normal adrenal function but in rare cases, adrenal insufficiency may be observed in the context of severe-early onset variants.\nsynonym: \"NR5A1-related sex development disorder\" EXACT [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005039 {source=\"PMID:28033660\", source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/\"} ! reproductive system disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005039 ! reproductive system disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7983 ! NR5A1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7983 {source=\"PMID:28033660\"} ! NR5A1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9863\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060212\nname: CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A syndromic disease caused by a variation in the CRYAB gene, and characterized by a spectrum of phenotypes including cardiomyopathy, cataract, and/or myopathy.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280, PMID:21920752, PMID:38212463]\nsynonym: \"alpha-B crystallinopathy\" RELATED [PMID:21920752]\nsynonym: \"CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! syndromic disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/2389 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! CRYAB\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9774\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060213\nname: reticular pseudodrusen\ndef: \"A retinal drusen characterized by subretinal deposits located internal to the retinal pigment epithelium, composed of material aggregations in the subretinal space between photoreceptors and the retinal pigment epithelium. These deposits have a bluish-white appearance by biomicroscopy and appear as hyperreflective lesions above the retinal pigment epithelium on optical coherence tomography.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489, PMID:29859199, PMID:38386332, PMID:41361163]\ncomment: Reticular pseudodrusen are a strong independent risk factor for late age-related macular degeneration and are particularly associated with geographic atrophy and type 3 neovascularization.\nsynonym: \"RPD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489, PMID:29859199]\nsynonym: \"SDD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489, PMID:29859199]\nsynonym: \"subretinal drusenoid deposit\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489, PMID:29859199, PMID:38386332]\nxref: SCTID:762533006 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0006949 {source=\"PMID:29859199\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\"} ! retinal drusen\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9849\" xsd:anyURI\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
